# components/builds
[[ if not .BuildRegistry ]]
**Builds are off on [[ .ClusterName ]]**: Infrared has no build registry (chart
value `builds.registry`, the operator's `INFRARED_BUILD_REGISTRY`), so every
file in this directory holds no objects and no Application points at it. Set
the registry and re-hydrate the template to turn builds on; the rest of this
page describes what then runs.
[[ else ]]
Builds push to **`[[ .BuildRegistry ]]`**.
[[ end ]]
Product image builds with [kpack](https://github.com/buildpacks-community/kpack)
on the management cluster. The `builds` Application (sync wave 26, right after
`kpack` at 25) syncs this directory:

| Object | What |
|---|---|
| Namespace `builds` | Pod Security `restricted`. Every product's kpack `Image`, and so every build pod, lives here. |
| Namespace `build-credentials` | ECR registries only. Pod Security `privileged`, for the ECR login job's hostNetwork (see `namespaces.yaml`). |
| ClusterStore `paketo` | Paketo `go`, `nodejs` and `web-servers` buildpacks, pinned by tag and digest. |
| ClusterStack `noble` | Paketo's Ubuntu 24.04 build and run images, pinned. |
| ClusterBuilder `infrared-builder` | Order `go`, `web-servers`, `nodejs`; pushed to `<build registry>/kpack-builder`. |
[[- if eq .Forge "gitea" ]]
| ServiceAccount `builds/builder` | What builds and the ClusterBuilder run as; lists `registry-push` and `gitea-git`. |
| CronJob `build-credentials/ecr-login` | ECR only: every 6h (and once per sync) writes `builds/registry-push` from the node's IAM role. |
[[- else ]]
| ServiceAccount `builds/builder` | What builds and the ClusterBuilder run as; lists `registry-push` and `github-git`. |
| CronJob `build-credentials/ecr-login` | ECR only: every 6h (and once per sync) writes `builds/registry-push` from the node's IAM role. |
| CronJob `builds/github-token` | Every 45m (and once per sync) writes `builds/github-git` and `builds/git-credentials` from Infrared's GitHub App for the org. |
[[- end ]]

## Registry credentials

`builds/registry-push` is a `kubernetes.io/dockerconfigjson` Secret with the
annotation `kpack.io/docker: <registry host>`.

- **ECR** (the build registry contains `.dkr.ecr.`): `ecr-login` writes it
  with a 12-hour token from the node's IAM role, which it reaches over the
  host network (IMDSv2, hop limit 1). The node role needs
  `ecr:GetAuthorizationToken` and push rights on the repositories below.
- **Any other registry**: nothing is rendered for it. The org creates the
  Secret itself (and later from Infisical), and keeps it current:

  ```bash
  kubectl -n builds create secret docker-registry registry-push \
    --docker-server=<registry host> --docker-username=<user> --docker-password=<token> \
    --dry-run=client -o yaml \
    | kubectl annotate --local -f - kpack.io/docker=<registry host> -o yaml \
    | kubectl apply --server-side -f -
  ```

**Repositories must exist before the first push**: ECR does not create them
on push. Create `<build registry>/kpack-builder` (the builder image) and one
`<build registry>/<product>` per product.

## Source credentials
[[ if eq .Forge "gitea" ]]
The org's repos are on Gitea, at `[[ .ForgeURL ]]`. kpack clones with
`builds/gitea-git`: `kubernetes.io/basic-auth`, the org's bot user with its
read-only token as the password, annotation `kpack.io/git: [[ .ForgeURL ]]`.
The operator writes it from the org's GitProvider `gitea` (Secret `gitea`,
key `read-token`, in namespace `ir-org-[[ .OrgName ]]`) once this namespace
exists, so nothing here makes a token, and there is no `github-token` job.
A build that fetches private dependencies itself has no `git-credentials`
binding on Gitea yet.
[[- else ]]
`github-token` signs a JWT for Infrared's own GitHub App for the org (App ID
and installation ID from the GitProvider `github`, private key from Secret
`github-app`, key `private-key.pem`, both in namespace
`ir-org-[[ .OrgName ]]`), exchanges it for an installation token limited to
`contents: read` and `metadata: read`, and server-side applies:

- `builds/github-git`: `kubernetes.io/basic-auth`, annotation
  `kpack.io/git: https://github.com`. kpack clones with it.
- `builds/git-credentials`: `service.binding/git-credentials` in the
  git-credential format Paketo's git buildpack reads. Bind it on an Image
  when the build itself fetches private dependencies (Go modules, npm git
  dependencies).

The App must be installed on the repositories a product builds from. Until
the org's App is installed (no installation ID yet) the job logs a notice and
succeeds; the next run picks it up.
[[- end ]]

## What a product adds

A kpack `Image` in namespace `builds`, built by `infrared-builder` as
`builder`, tagged `<build registry>/<product>`. It lives in the gitops repo at
`products/<product>/build/image.yaml` (see the repo README, "Products"):

```yaml
apiVersion: kpack.io/v1alpha2
kind: Image
metadata:
  name: <product>
  namespace: builds
spec:
  tag: [[ if .BuildRegistry ]][[ .BuildRegistry ]][[ else ]]<build registry>[[ end ]]/<product>
  serviceAccountName: builder
  builder:
    kind: ClusterBuilder
    name: infrared-builder
  source:
    git:
      url: [[ if eq .Forge "gitea" ]][[ .ForgeURL ]]/<owner>/<repo>.git[[ else ]]https://github.com/<owner>/<repo>[[ end ]]
      revision: main
  build:
    # Only when the build fetches private dependencies itself.
    services:
      - apiVersion: v1
        kind: Secret
        name: git-credentials
    # For a UI served by nginx:
    # env:
    #   - name: BP_WEB_SERVER
    #     value: nginx
    #   - name: BP_NODE_RUN_SCRIPTS
    #     value: build
```
